# --- DISCOVERIES 10-24 (optional, no quest needs them): diver's cache + slate + air pocket; TP_SnowVehicle01 + chest; hatch with a chest; buried treasure; viewpoint ---
place "Box Small" dcampbox at 5.6 35.6 ground sit
place Note_Paper dnote at 5.6 35.6 ground y=0.7 drop yaw=30
place Loot_ChestSmall dcamp at 7.6 37.1 ground sit yaw=77
call airpocket x=3.1 z=33.6 id=seed_ark_dair al=dairzone bub=dairbub r=2.5 msg="Air trapped in a diver's bell-tent. Breathe."
note dnote Diver's slate | (chalked on a diver's slate, tied to a box)\n\nCOLD. TOO COLD FOR LONG DIVES. AIR IN THE ROOMS ONLY.\nThat was the diver before me. The rest is mine.\nFirst dive: the flood door, the shaft, the lamps still burning thirty metres down. Somebody kept them going a long time.\nSecond dive: room 4 and the valve. It will not turn. Dead pumps, the engineer's log says, and the islet's halls are too far for these hands.\nThird dive: I am going down to sit with the valve a while. If it moves, it moves.\nThe dogs are fed. The goats are somebody else's now.\n\n- O. V.
note dcamp Diver's cache | A diver's spare kit, wired shut against the current.
loot dcamp Rope*2;Glass*3;Plastic*4
prop dcamp loot.refill=0
place TP_SnowVehicle01 dvan at -6.1 -38.5 ground yaw=197
prop dvan tint.color=#8a9aa6
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at -10.1 -35.5 ground sit yaw=137
note dwreckchest Frozen chest | Frozen to the runner: wool, rope and a tin of nails.
loot dwreckchest Wool*3;Rope*2;Nail*8
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=36.9 z=-12.7 r=15 seed=13091 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;Wool*3;Bolt*2
call vinecache x=-12.7 z=-36.9 r=15 seed=13093 chest=dvinechest vines=dvines items=Rope*3;Wool*2;Bolt*3
call treasure x=-36.9 z=12.7 r=15 n=1 seed=13092
prop treasure13092 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;MetalOre*2
# REDO 10-24 TREASURE2: a second buried treasure on the far side for the detector + shovel
call treasure x=29.5 z=-10.2 r=12 n=1 seed=13142
prop treasure13142 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*1;MetalOre*2;TradeToken*2
place Zone_Trigger dview at -33.4 -20.1 ground y=1.5
prop dview zone.id=seed_ark_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=The pressure rooms lie in a row along the ridge below, lights still on in some of them.

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# the generator's rocks that floated over the slope (ground check, 2026-10-23)
clear at -0.91 24.6 r=1.5 only=TP_BigRock

info title=The Seed Ark
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Coldhold's lowest level, flooded 30 m down: pressure rooms with air under their roofs, long halls of seed racks, a gate of ice, white anglers - and the ark valve that finishes what the vault began. The last island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||Far below, lamps still burn along a row of drowned rooms.

story arkvalve|The ark valve|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The Seed Ark's valve, turned. The Coldhold's way is finished.

# --- DEEP 10-24: the pumps, the cooling rods, the valves ---
story coolrod|A cooling rod|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A cooling rod from a flooded hall, for the pump station's sockets.
story rodset|A cooling rod set|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A cooling rod set in the pump station's socket.
story pumpkey|The pump key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The pump key: it unlocks the islet's three valves.
story valveturned|A valve turned|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|One of the pump islet's three valves, opened.
story pumpsrun|The pumps running|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The Ark's pumps run again: the ark valve can turn.
note engineerlog Pump engineer's log | PUMP ENGINEER'S LOG\n\nThe ark valve will not turn on dead pumps. It was built that way, so nobody floods the racks by accident. I hate whoever built it that way, and it was me.\nThe pump switch stands on the islet south-east, by the cooling station - the only rock over the water. When the coolant began to boil I took the three cooling rods out and hid one in each cooling hall: east, west and north. Nobody steals what nobody can reach.\nThe station keeps the pump key until its rods are home. Then the three valves out in the rotten gas, and only then the switch. Wear a suit from the cabinets. And mind the rats: they live in the pipes, and they think the pipes are theirs.\n\n- B. Moe, pump engineer
note rodchest1 East hall rod chest | Flooded east hall: a cooling rod in its lead sleeve.
loot rodchest1 story:coolrod*1;CopperIngot*2
note rodchest2 West hall rod chest | Flooded west hall: a cooling rod and the hall keeper's spares.
loot rodchest2 story:coolrod*1;Bolt*3;Glass*2
note rodchest3 North hall rod chest | A chest in the flooded north hall: the last cooling rod.
loot rodchest3 story:coolrod*1;MetalIngot*2
note pumpchest Pump keeper's chest | The pump keeper's chest: dry clothes, tools, seeds he kept himself.
loot pumpchest TitaniumIngot*1;Seed_Pine*3;Rope*2
prop pumpchest loot.refill=0
prop treasure13151 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;CopperOre*2
prop treasure13152 treasure.loot=MetalOre*3;TradeToken*3
prop sock1 obj.name=sock1
prop sock2 obj.name=sock2
prop sock3 obj.name=sock3
prop sock1 beh.use=Set a cooling rod in the socket
prop sock1 if.use=!signal|sock1\ntake|story:coolrod|1
prop sock1 on.use=signal||sock1\ngive||story:rodset*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The cooling rod slides home in its socket.
prop sock1 else.use=message||An empty socket for a cooling rod. The pump engineer's log (pressure room 4) says where the rods are.
prop sock2 beh.use=Set a cooling rod in the socket
prop sock2 if.use=!signal|sock2\ntake|story:coolrod|1
prop sock2 on.use=signal||sock2\ngive||story:rodset*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The cooling rod slides home in its socket.
prop sock2 else.use=message||An empty socket for a cooling rod. The pump engineer's log (pressure room 4) says where the rods are.
prop sock3 beh.use=Set a cooling rod in the socket
prop sock3 if.use=!signal|sock3\ntake|story:coolrod|1
prop sock3 on.use=signal||sock3\ngive||story:rodset*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The cooling rod slides home in its socket.
prop sock3 else.use=message||An empty socket for a cooling rod. The pump engineer's log (pressure room 4) says where the rods are.
prop pumplever obj.name=pumplever
prop pumplever beh.use=Pull the cooling station's lever
prop pumplever if.use=!signal|pumpkey\ntake|story:rodset|3
prop pumplever on.use=signal||pumpkey\ngive||story:pumpkey*1\nsound||event:/exploring/temperence/selene/reactor_alarm\nmessage||The station shudders, the cooling jams - an alarm - and the emergency release drops the pump key into your hand.
prop pumplever else.use=message||The lever won't move: the cooling station has three empty rod sockets.
prop valve1 obj.name=valve1
prop valve1 beh.use=Open the valve
prop valve1 if.use=has|story:pumpkey|1\n!signal|valve1
prop valve1 on.use=signal||valve1\ngive||story:valveturned*1\nshow|rats1\nsound||event:/exploring/temperence/selene/reactor_alarm\nmessage||The valve groans open - and out of the pipes behind it, rats!
prop valve1 else.use=message||The valve is locked to the cooling station. Its lever gives the pump key.
