prop pumpswitch beh.use=Throw the pump switch
prop pumpswitch if.use=!signal|pumpsrun\ntake|story:valveturned|3\ntake|story:pumpkey|1
prop pumpswitch on.use=signal||pumpsrun\ngive||story:pumpsrun*1\nsound||event:/exploring/temperence/selene/reactor_alarm\nmessage||Deep under the sea the pumps cough, then thunder. The Ark's water starts to move.
prop pumpswitch else.use=message||The pump switch is dead: the islet's three valves are shut.

note manifest Ark manifest | THE SEED ARK - MANIFEST (kept by the gardener)\n\nRacks 1-40: grains. 41-80: fruit and tree seed. 81-96: flowers, for the bees, when there are bees again. I argued for the bees a whole winter. The council said bees do not eat. I said neither will you, when the bees are gone.\nPressure rooms 1-4 hold air for the keepers. The ice gate opens from room 1 for about forty breaths, then it shuts under its own weight. Count them. Do not argue with it; I did, and lost a boot.\nEach room keeps an ark seal in its box under the roof. The valve wants all three before it will hear you.\nThe lamps down the halls were meant to burn for ever. They do not. When the valve turns, they come back on, one hall at a time.\n\n- M. Lunde, gardener
note ringwavefile The Ringwave file | THE RINGWAVE - FILE (the founders' archivist)\n\nThe founders did not invent the sign. They found it cut in stone on the Coldhold's sea doors and on the glacier wall, and in the old charts beside one word: ENGINE.\nThe charts put the engine in the south, past the last ice, where the sea runs warm and wrong. Ships that went to look sent one message each and then nothing. The Warden reads that as a warning. I read it as a map.\nOn the low band, some nights, there is a slow pulse from that way, once a minute. It is not a voice. It is something running.\nThe founders cut the ring and the wave over our door so the keepers would remember: whatever it is, it is still running, and one day somebody will have to go and look. Not me. My knees are bad.\n\n- S. Dahl, archivist
note closingnote The closing note | (the radio's teleprinter woke with the pumps and typed this, line after line)\n\nSEED ARK LIVE. ALL STATIONS.\nFROM THE WHALE, H. BRASK: Valve heard. Under way south in the launch, toward the pulse. If something down there counts lights, let it count mine first. Choose for the ones still talking.\nFROM SAGA DRIFT: Good morning, Ice! Sparks here, back on the air, and the council can fine me in penguins. Caller 1: you. Best caller ever.\nFROM STEAMVENT: Ivo of the relay, in with the sealers. The stack listens again. I heard bells the night the mast bent. Now I know whose.\nFROM THE COLDHOLD, O. FENN: The Warden is answered. Whatever was chosen in the vault, the Ark heard it, and the sky did not fall. We are opening the doors.\nTO ORRIN VALE, COURIER: delivered.\n\nThe surface hole is straight up. Go home - and then south.
note orrinletter Orrin's last letter | (in a tin inside the dead man's coat)\n\nTo Hedda Brask, if she lives. To Ivo, to Sparks, to anybody.\nI was the Warden's courier. Every letter of his silence went out in my friendly post, sealed, between your parcels and your birthday cards. I took the sealers' set for repair and sank it off the floe. On day 19 I bent the stack's guys in the dark, and Ivo heard my bells and blamed the wind. On day 31 I cut the Whale's line with my own hatchet, the one with the dog's head. Hedda, you gave me your last coffee that week.\nHe paid me with a berth. A bunk in the Coldhold, warm and quiet, while the rest of you went dark one by one.\nI came down to wake the Ark, because it was the one thing left I could put right. The valve will not move. The pumps are dead, and so, near enough, am I. The cold is in my hands now.\nTuva and Knut ran home. Somebody feed them.\nWhoever reads this: wake the pumps, turn the valve, and tell them all I am sorry. Tell Sparks to talk as loud as he likes.\n\n- Orrin Vale, courier
prop closingnote beh.hidden=1

